1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:03,930
They say agriculture is the backbone of Ghana's economy.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,860
Let's put that to the test. Three numbers.

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:10,800
Number one: jobs.

4
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:15,930
Out of every hundred working Ghanaians, about thirty-seven work in agriculture.

5
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:18,580
That's around five million people.

6
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:20,500
That's a backbone.

7
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:23,290
Number two: output.

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:31,160
Out of every hundred cedis of economic output produced in 2025, about twenty-three came from agriculture.

9
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,140
Still a backbone.

10
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:36,760
Number three: bank loans.

11
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:46,970
At the end of 2025, out of every hundred cedis Ghana's banks had outstanding in loans, just over four cedis were in agriculture.

12
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:48,410
Four.

13
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:52,280
You might think that's because agriculture is shrinking.

14
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:53,720
It isn't.

15
00:00:54,060 --> 00:01:01,970
In 2025, agriculture grew by 6.8 percent, faster than the economy's overall growth of 6 percent.

16
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:03,990
And here's what's interesting.

17
00:01:04,910 --> 00:01:07,510
Bank loans to agriculture actually went up.

18
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:11,000
But bank loans overall went up faster.

19
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:16,920
So agriculture's share fell, from 4.7 percent to 4.3 percent.

20
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:22,550
Now, these are bank loans, not every source of financing agriculture relies on.

21
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:26,260
So, is agriculture the backbone of Ghana's economy?

22
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:29,010
Of its jobs? Yes.

23
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:31,800
Of its output? Yes.

24
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:35,250
But of the loans sitting on Ghana's banks' books?

25
00:01:36,010 --> 00:01:38,550
A little over four cedis in every hundred.

26
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,490
Even in a year agriculture outgrew the economy.

27
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:44,560
Unpacked by GilB.

28
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,660
There's more to the story.
